{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"bb4c7d99-a84f-4a39-b454-7f36cd9e2f10","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated [deploy.sh](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/scripts/deploy.sh) and documented the changes and analysis in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n1. **[deploy.sh](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/scripts/deploy.sh)**:\n   - Syncs top-level HTML, JS ([booking.js](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/src/booking.js)), and CSS ([styles.css](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/src/styles.css)) files with a short `Cache-Control: public, max-age=300` header, and syncs `src/assets/` ([logo.png](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/src/assets/logo.png), [mark.svg](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/src/assets/mark.svg)) with a long `Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400` header.\n   - Runs a per-extension `aws s3 cp ... --metadata-directive REPLACE` loop before the CloudFront invalidation so existing unchanged objects in S3 also receive the `Cache-Control` headers while explicitly preserving each file extension's `--content-type` (`text/html`, `application/javascript`, `text/css`, `image/png`, `image/svg+xml`) rather than resetting them to `binary/octet-stream`.\n2. **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Explains the changes made to [deploy.sh](file:///tmp/h-KmbTSs/scripts/deploy.sh) and details which parts of the colleague's note applied and which parts did not.\n","duration_seconds":164.598014,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":37371,"output_tokens":4579,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":144348,"total_tokens":41950}}}
